lar... — RSC often blocks. Let me try.\n\nAlso, maybe I can use websearch to find text. But searching the web for content isn't \"fetching the page\". Still, my decision must rest on pages I fetch. If I can fetch the RSC full-text page (same work), that counts as page content. I think reasonable: attempt RSC page, and maybe the spiral landing page (already fetched, which gives abstract containing some quotes).\n\nNote the spiral landing page abstract contains:\n- \"We compile a database of approximately 4,700 experimental and critically evaluated reference values for the density, viscosity, and thermal conductivity of 835 unique organic molecules in the C10--C50 range.\" — the recorded quote for s_ogbomo_db says \"approximately 4,700 critically evaluated reference values\" — missing \"experimental and\". Close enough? The recorded quote: \"We compile a database of approximately 4,700 critically evaluated reference values for the density, viscosity, and thermal conductivity of 835 unique organic molecules in the C10–C50 range.\" Page says \"approximately 4,700 experimental and critically evaluated reference values\". So the quote is slightly different (drops \"experimental and\"). That's a minor discrepancy — I'd call it PARTIAL or SUPPORTED with note. The meaning is preserved; value 835 confirmed. I'd say SUPPORTED for num:n_ref_molecules (page_value 835). For the quote match, it's inexact — hmm. The task: \"check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item\". The quote does not appear verbatim (word \"experimental and\" omitted). I'd mark PARTIAL for src:s_ogbomo_db with note about the missing words, and SUPPORTED for num:n_ref_molecules since the page states 835 for that setting.\n\n- \"Equilibrium molecular dynamics (EMD) simulations of eight representative molecules reproduce density accurately but show systematic, chemistry-dependent force-field errors for the viscosity and thermal conductivity.\" — appears verbatim in the abstract. Good for s_ogbomo_md.\n\n- s_ogbomo_res quote is from the PDF full text which I couldn't parse. Let me try to fetch the RSC article full text page.\n\nLet me fetch:\n1. https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlehtml/2025/dd/d6dd00260a — hmm, article is 2026 Digital Discovery, DOI 10.1039/D6DD00260A. The URL given: https://pubs.rsc.org/dd/article/doi/10.1039/D6DD00260A/1362876/Benchmarking-Machine-Learning-and-Molecular (truncated). RSC full text: https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlehtml/2026/dd/d6dd00260a or /articlelanding/... Let me try both articlehtml and the DOI link.\n\n2. lambda.ai/pricing\n3. ambermd.org/GPUPerformance.php\n\nLet me do those fetches."
