cogenides with intrinsically low thermal\\nconductivity as they continue to be of interest for electronics and energy-related applications.\\nKeywords: Quaternary chalcogenide, lattice disorder, thermal properties, low thermal conductivity\\n* Email: gnolas@usf.edu\\n2\\nINTRODUCTION\\nAr environment. The maximum experimental uncertainty in the 𝛼𝑡ℎ measurements was 5 %. The\\ntemperature-dependent thermal conductivity, 𝜅, was calculated using the relationship 𝜅 = 𝐷𝛼𝑡ℎ𝐶𝑝,\\nwhere D is the measured density of the specimen. At high temperature, 𝐶𝑝 ≈ 𝐶𝑣, the isochoric\\nMorelli, G. Slack, High lattice thermal conductivity solids. In High thermal conductivity\\nmaterials, Springer, New York, 2006.\\n[70] S.M. Wasim, Transport properties of CuInSe2, Sol. Cells. 16 (1986) 289–316.\\nhttps://doi.org/10.1016/0379-6787(86)90091-8.\\n[71] Wasim S. M., Thermal conductivity of ternary compounds, Phys. Status Solidi. 51 (1979) K35–\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"warnings\": null,\n  \"metadata\": null,\n  \"session_id\": \"ses_eb2cf42ecffelQwcJMJg9gUryT\"\n}"
